l lives of consumers in Poland.\",6\r\n301,POS,\"Point of Sale (POS) systems are essential tools used for processing card transactions in physical retail environments. In Poland, these systems have demonstrated a steady increase in usage from 2017 to 2021. This growth trend was notably influenced by the COVID-19 pandemic, during which there was a significant rise in card transactions. The pandemic accelerated the adoption of cashless payment methods, as consumers and businesses alike sought safer and more convenient transaction options. As a result, POS systems have become increasingly integral to the retail experience, facilitating efficient and secure payment processing.\",3\r\n295,PAYMENT CARDS,\"Payment cards are physical or virtual cards used to make transactions, including credit, debit, and prepaid cards\",2\r\n296,VIRTUAL DIGITAL WALLETS,Virtual digital wallets are online services or apps that store payment information and allow users to make electronic transactions,2\r\n290,MOBILE BANKING MARKET IN POLAND,\"The analysis of the mobile banking market in Poland centers on the use and development of mobile applications and cashless payment systems over the period from 2017 to 2021. This market study involves the creation of specific indicators designed to measure and compare the utilization of mobile applications against other forms of cashless payment systems. By focusing on these aspects, the analysis provides insights into the trends and shifts in consumer behavior regarding mobile banking and cashless transactions within Poland during this timeframe. The study aims to offer a comprehensive understanding of how mobile banking applications are being adopted and how they stack up against other cashless payment methods, reflecting the evolving landscape of financial technology in Poland.\",9\r\n10,BLIKA,\"BLIKA is a mobile payment system used in Poland, offering various functionalities for banking transactions\",2\r\n13,ZWIĄZEK BANKÓW POLSKICH,\"Związek Banków 